ing costs\nFunding\nFunding overview\nDoctoral training programmes\nExternal funding and loans\nColleges\nColleges overview\nCollege listing\nAccommodation\nCollege Visit Days\nApplying\nApplying overview\nApplication deadlines\nBefore you apply\nEntry requirements\nInternational qualifications\nEnglish language requirements\nFind a supervisor\nWidening access and participation\nHow to apply\nSupporting documents\nReferences\nApplication fee\nInternational applications\nDisabled applicants\nVisiting students\nTransferring from another university\nAI and postgraduate applications\nAdmissions fraud\nAfter you apply\nHow we assess your application\nInterviews\nOutcome of your application\nYour offer\nChanging your start date to a later term\nDeferring your offer to the next academic year\nPrepare to arrive\nTrack your application\nInternational\nInternational overview\nHow to apply\nInternational qualifications\nEnglish language requirements\nVisas and immigration\nInternational visits and events\nStudent views\nAkhila\u2019s story\nAlex\u2019s story\nHuijie\u2019s story\nKelsey\u2019s story\nLu\u2019s story\nNilesh\u2019s story\nGet in touch!\nEvents\nEvents overview\nPostgraduate Open Days\nDiscover Cambridge webinars\nInternational visits and events\nGetting here\nContact us\nEntry requirements\nMain menu\nApplying\nApplication deadlines\nBefore you apply\nEntry requirements\nInternational qualifications\nEnglish language requirements\nFind a supervisor\nWidening access and participation\nHow to apply\nAfter you apply\nTrack your application\nWhy Cambridge\nCourses\nFinance\nFunding\nColleges\nInternational\nEvents\nContact us\nWe encourage applicants with the best academic potential to apply for our courses.\nBefore starting your application, it's essential to review the entry requirements for your chosen course.\nAcademic requirements\nYou can check the entry requirements for your course in the Course Directory.\nThe University\u2019s minimum academic requirement is a 2:1 (upper second class) UK Bachelor's Honours Degree or international equivalent.\nA pass in a UK Master\u2019s Degree (or equivalent) or a higher degree exceeds the University's minimum requirement and is therefore accepted.\nPlease note that many of our courses require a higher standard, such as a High 2:1, a First, or a UK Master's degree.\nInternational qualifications\nIf your qualifications are from outside the UK, you should check our international qualifications page to ensure they meet the requirements for your course.\nEnglish language requirements\nIf English is not your first language, you may need to demonstrate that you meet the English language requirements for your course.\nCheck the English language requirements page for details on:\nWhether you need to take a test\nWhen to take your test\nHow to submit your results\nFinancial requirements\nWhen you take a postgraduate degree, you need to cover costs like course fees and living costs.\nBefore starting your course, you'll need to confirm that you can meet these costs for the duration of the course. You do not need to do this unless we make you an offer of a place. If you have already secured funding, you can give us those details in your application.\nYou may want to apply for funding to help you cover your costs. Look for funding using the University\u2019s funding search website.\nAdmissions fraud\nWe take admissions fraud seriously. All applications are thoroughly checked for fake documents and false information. Find out what happens if your application is found to be fraudulent.\nApplicant Portal\nCreate, manage and track your postgraduate application.\nLog in\nRelated Links\nCheck your course requirements\nInternational qualifications\nEnglish language requirements\nPostgraduate Admissions Office\nAbout us\nAdmissions statistics\nStart an application\nApplicant Self-Service\nContact us\nAbout this site\nAbout our website\nCookie notice\nPrivacy policy\nEvent booking policy\nUniversity Poli